@@ -29,6 +29,8 @@ Loaded by Rules Core at startup; indexes all card/terrain/map/Champion definitio
 ### Card Editor tool
 A separate authoring tool, not part of the shipped runtime, that reads/writes the same JSON files. The JSON format is the source of truth; the editor is a convenience layer over it. It must not become the *only* way to produce a valid card file (e.g. by being built as an engine-editor-only plugin with its own serialization) — that would silently reintroduce an engine-specific dependency and undermine the portability constraint (A5) this component exists to protect.
 
+**Current state (provisional schema):** the catalog lives in `content/cards/<id>.json`, one file per card. `tools/Leyline.DebugUi/wwwroot/cards.html` is the editor, with read/write going through `Leyline.Content.Json.CardCatalog`. The editor's field schema is the `FIELDS`/`TYPES` table at the top of `cards.js`. Properties the schema doesn't cover are kept untouched on save, so card files survive schema changes. Each card has an editor-only `comment` that the engine ignores. Saving is refused for types the engine can't load yet (Companion, Structure, Item, Map, Terrain).
+
 ## Open dependency
 
 This component cannot be fully specified until Track A finishes:
