+  Kept separate because the main checkout has another session's uncommitted Track A (D83) work.
+- **Everything is uncommitted.** Run `git status` in the worktree to see it. All 134 tests pass (`dotnet test Leyline.slnx`).
+- **Run it:** `dotnet run --project tools/Leyline.DebugUi` from the worktree, then open http://localhost:5299 and click "Card creator"
+  (or go to `/cards.html` directly). Port 5299 is hardcoded, so only one DebugUi can run at a time.
+
+## What was built (phase 1: card creator)
+
+- **Catalog:** `content/cards/<id>.json`, one pretty-printed file per card. Seeded with the 4 engine cards
+  (`test.champion`, `test.grunt`, `test.firebolt`, `test.mend`), same ids as the scenario files.
+- **`Leyline.Content.Json.CardCatalog`:** list/save/delete using raw JSON objects. Unknown properties survive a save.
+  Every save is checked with the engine's own parser. Ids are unique ignoring case, compared against the id
+  *inside* each file. Saving is refused for types the engine can't load yet (Companion, Structure, Item, Map, Terrain).
+- **`JsonCardDefinitionRepository.LoadFromDirectory`** now rejects duplicate ids (ignoring case).
+- **DebugUi:**
+  - Endpoints: `GET/PUT/DELETE /api/catalog/cards`.
+  - Page: `wwwroot/cards.html|js|css`, linked from the hub.
+  - Left pane: pick a type, see that type's cards, filter them.
+  - Right pane: a form built from the `FIELDS`/`TYPES` table at the top of `cards.js` (the one place to update when
+    Track A adds properties). Also: comment field, "Other properties" JSON box, raw JSON mode, Copy/Revert,
+    two-step Delete, live warning when an id is already taken.
+- **Tests:** `tests/Leyline.RulesCore.Tests/TestSupport/CardCatalogTests.cs`;
+  `tests/Leyline.Scenarios.Tests/CardCatalogContentTests.cs` (the catalog must load, and must match the inline `card` lines in the DebugUi scenarios).
+- **Docs:** `docs/architecture/card-data-and-editor.md` has a "Current state" paragraph.
+
+## Decisions agreed with the user
+
+- Readable string ids stay; auto-numbered ids were discussed and rejected, because scenario/deck files must stay readable by hand.
+  Ids must be unique.
+- Card types: deck types are Creature, Companion, Structure, Item, Spell; special types are Champion, Map, Terrain.
+  Types the engine doesn't support show "not implemented yet".
+- Each card has a `comment`: written to the file, shown in the editor, never shown in the game.
+- The format must stay easy to fix, because the card properties will keep changing along with Track A.
+- The editor starts with the fields the engine supports today; it grows together with Track A.
